<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muziris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muziris was an ancient port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malabar-coast">Malabar Coast</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, probably near modern Pattanam in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>. In the early centuries CE it was the main harbour of the Chera kingdom and a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> trade with Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periplus-of-the-erythraean-sea">Periplus of the Erythraean Sea</a> and the Muziris <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a>. It declined after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periyar-river">Periyar River</a> shifted course, traditionally in the 14th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muziris.jpg" alt="Muziris" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TabulaPeutingerianaMuziris.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
